Z||000000||FieroMaster88||03-18-2001||11:34 PM||||Well, it has been about a month and a half now since I have driven my 88......the trans died on me and I have been rebuilding it at school.   I installed a Fiero Store shift kit, painted the brackets and have bunches of otehr stuff to install.  Well, the trans is back in the car and tomorow I finish it up.  I wonder what it feels like to drive a Fiero, i dont remember.  Either way, i am very excited........<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">       <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/3dlil/eek2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||mrfiero||03-18-2001||11:52 PM||||Is this your 30K mile coupe?  What in the world happened to your tranny that caused it to poop out?  I'm just curious (maybe I missed that post), but I have never had an auto. tranny die on me.  In fact, I have a Formula pushing 200K miles and it is just fine.<P>At any rate, good luck with it......it will drive a lot differently, since you haven't driven it in so long.  I have been driving a truck for the past few weeks and I drove one of my Formulas the other day and was amazed at how it drove (it was nice!).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||5
Z||000002||MooCow||03-19-2001||12:10 AM||||Congrats on your car finally getting done.<BR>Yea why did the tranny die??<BR>It will be so different driving the Fiero after been gone for so long.  After I drive my Fiero around for a bit and then get into the Ranger it feels like the Ranger is a monster truck.  Hope to your Fiero soon.  Mine should be done soon I hope.<P>                             Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny.  Soon will be Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||03-19-2001||12:27 AM||||Well, the tranny went partly because of being stored so long by the previous owner and because a seal on the driect clutch apply piston was folded, happened from the factory, i guess GM had a problem with them doing that....according to my instructor.  I never knew there was sooo much to an automatic trans.  Geesh, it was a pain to put back together but I am happy i could do it myself.  Saved about $1000!  I put $250 worth of parts in it, thats all.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">       <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/3dlil/eek2.gif"> ||||reg||1
